tatistical Office [Zambia], and ORC Macro</collab></person-group><source>Zambia HIV/AIDS Service Provision Assessment Survey 2005</source><year>2006</year><publisher-name>Calverton, Maryland, USA: Ministry of Health</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>ACQUIRE Project</collab></person-group><source>Moving family planning programs forward: learning from success in Zambia, Malawi, and Ghana</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>New York: The ACQUIRE Project/Engender Health</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>No authors listed</collab></person-group><article-title>Zambia project serving as African model</article-title><source>JOICFP News</source><year>1997</year><volume>280</volume><fpage>7</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12292747</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Central Statistical Office (CSO) [Zambia], Central Board of Health [Zambia], and ORC Marco</collab></person-group><source>Zambia Demographic and Health Survey, 2001&#x02013;2002</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>Calverton, Maryland, USA: CSO, CBH, and ORC Macro</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rutstein</surname><given-names>SO</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The DHS Wealth Index</article-title><source>DHS Comparative Reports</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>Calverton, Maryland: ORC Macro</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Central Statistical Office (CSO) [Zambia]</collab></person-group><source>2000 census of population and housing</source><year>2001</ye